{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And the master of the house shall be brought near to Elohim... the matter of them both shall come before Elohim... whom Elohim shall condemn.</b> He mentioned here 'Elohim' three times, and from this the Rabbis of blessed memory derived that a court may not be fewer than three. And you will not find in all the laws of the parashah from the beginning of the book until here that he mentions the special Name, but only the name Elohim — and the reason for this is that judgment belongs to Elohim. But in the matter of the oath he mentioned the special Name and said 'an oath of YHWH,' and this is clear because the central line is the essence of the oath, and therefore he attributed the oath to the special Name. And behold, the word שבועת is missing a vav, written שבעת, for it is derived from שבעה, and this has already been mentioned and repeated."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:02:53.974063166Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}